+# Current checkpoint metadata repair
+
+**Goal:** Prevent receipt reconciliation from retaining an obsolete execution date or obsolete synchronization aliases.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the existing pure checkpoint reconciler and all receipt/digest gates. Derive the current audit date from the validated daily ledger. Normalize source and remote commit aliases from the current synchronization snapshot, retaining compatibility with older snapshot formats. Never infer a successful deployment or delivery from these metadata fields.
+
+**Scope:** `scripts/campaign-checkpoint-state.mjs` and focused synthetic regressions in `tests/campaign-checkpoint-state.test.mjs`. Historical evidence and real campaign receipts stay unchanged.
+
+1. Add regressions for an obsolete audit date and new-format synchronization keys conflicting with historical aliases; verify they fail.
+2. Prefer the current snapshot's canonical commit keys and normalize legacy aliases consistently; update only the audit execution date from the validated daily date.
+3. Run the checkpoint and receipt-generator tests. Validate real campaign/daily/continuation reconciliation read-only without changing any receipt or exclusions.
+4. Apply separately reviewed private metadata corrections backed by the verified 84-receipt proof. Publish exact source and anonymous safe-code synchronization, preserving the existing owner-private audience.
+
+No new send, daemon, credential, mailbox-health or authentication-restoration claim is authorized by this repair. A changed receipt digest still invalidates current remote coverage.
